4.Rearrange the order of widgets inside your Column so that the Button appears at the top, followed by the two Text widgets.
Run the app and describe how the UI changes.


import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(MaterialApp(
    home: Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: Text("My App"),
      ),
      body: Center(
        child: Column(
          mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
          children: [
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: () {},
              child: Text("Click Me"),
            ),
            Text("My Favorite Food: Pizza"),
            Text("My Favorite IPL Team: CSK"),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    ),
  ));
}

UI Changes

Before:

My Favorite Food: Pizza
My Favorite IPL Team: CSK
[ Click Me ]

After:

[ Click Me ]
My Favorite Food: Pizza
My Favorite IPL Team: CSK

Description: The Button now appears at the top, followed by the favorite food and IPL team text. 
The order of widgets in a Column determines the order in which they appear vertically on the screen.
